   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Spider%27s_Lullabye",
   "resumo_en": "The Spider's Lullabye is the sixth studio album by Danish heavy metal band King Diamond, released on 6 June 1995. Unlike other King Diamond albums, it is not a full concept album; only half the songs form a single plot. \nThe album was recorded after a four-year hiatus and this is the first release to feature guitarist Herb Simonsen, bassist Chris Estes and drummer Darrin Anthony. It is also the band's first release on Metal Blade Records. Guitarist Andy LaRocque said it was the most difficult King Diamond album to record because \"we had a new band [and] we had a totally new environment recording in the U.S., with a totally different producer.\" \nThe album was remastered by LaRocque and re-released in 2009.",
